pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `wiplvl` naming a level no rule ever established used to index past the end
% of `context.level_ids` and abort the process (release is `panic = "abort"`),
% i.e. a crash on ordinary proof text. It is now a checking error. A `wiplvl`
% of a level that WAS established stays valid -- see the companion instance
% wipe_level_established under correct/version3.
f 1;
wiplvl 7;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
